  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 14,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.597,
            0.071,
            0.812,
            0.088
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Two Variables, One Line"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.853,
            0.071,
            0.88,
            0.086
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "99"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.11,
            0.882,
            0.195
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "But why does "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ } ^ { \\circ } m ^ { \\flat }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " represent the slope? To understand this let us consider two points "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A } ( x _ { 1 } , y _ { 1 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { B }   ( x _ { _ 2 } ,   y _ { _ 2 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " which lie on the line "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = m x + d ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Since they satisfy the equation we get, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y_{1} = mx_{1} + d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y_{2} = mx_{2} + d."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.197,
            0.83,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, the slope of the line passing through the points A and B is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.218,
            0.798,
            0.258
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{y_{2}-y_{1}}{X_{2}-X_{1}}=\\frac{(mx_{2}+d)-(mx_{1}+d)}{X_{2}-X_{1}}=\\frac{mx_{2}-mx_{1}}{X_{2}-X_{1}}=\\frac{m(x_{2}-x_{1})}{x_{2}-x_{1}}=m"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.26,
            0.882,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This is the reason why we can just read off the slope of a line if its equation is in the form "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = m x + d ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " This also shows that the slope m of a line with equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = m x + d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is given by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { y _ { _ 2 } - y _ { _ 1 } } { X _ { _ 2 } - X _ { _ 1 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for any two points "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( x _ { 1 } , y _ { 1 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( x _ { \\mathrm { { 2 } } } , y _ { \\mathrm { { 2 } } } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on the line, regardless of which points they are."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.374,
            0.881,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note that the standard form of the equation of a line "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax + by + c = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " can be rewritten as"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.417,
            0.691,
            0.454
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "by = -ax - c   or   y = -\\frac{a}{b}x - \\frac{c}{b}, (b \\neq 0)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.46,
            0.881,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "which is of the form "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = m x + d ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Here "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "m = - \\frac{a}{b} \\bmod d = - \\frac{c}{b}."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Hence "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = mx + d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is another form of expressing the linear equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax + by + c = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , provided "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b \\neq 0 ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.548,
            0.881,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the line "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5x + y = 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Rewrite it as y = –5x + 3. Can you now find its slope? What does it mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.593,
            0.881,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = - 5x + 3, m = - 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the slope, which means for every increase of 1 unit in x, y decreases by 5 units. d = 3 is the y-intercept which means the line crosses the y-axis at (0, 3)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.658,
            0.661,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us make a table of values to draw its graph."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.22,
            0.683,
            0.778,
            0.745
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 12,
              "bbox": [
                0.22,
                0.683,
                0.778,
                0.745
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_table_12.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>x</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>-1</td></tr><tr><td>y</td><td>3</td><td>-2</td><td>8</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.757,
            0.88,
            0.799
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Plotting the ordered pairs A (0, 3), B (1, –2), C (–1, 8) and drawing the line through them we get the graph of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = - 5x + 3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.817,
            0.399,
            0.84
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.857,
            0.852,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you use the points A, B and C to verify that the slope of this line is indeed –5?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
